IMPORT prelude

-- Singapore Polytechnic Act 1954 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a student, a fee-payer, a diploma holder or a counterparty:
-- which instrument governs admission, awards, fees and discipline and how it must be made (ss 7(3)(d), (e), 23), late-payment
-- charges and the validation of past ones (ss 7(3)(e)(v), 7A), execution under the common seal (s 12), the Students' Union fee and
-- the Societies Act (ss 15, 16), borrowing (s 11(1)), the Board's size, terms, vacancies and votes (ss 4, 5, 6, 9), the Principal at
-- committees and removal of the Principal (s 14(1), (4)), inspection of committee records (s 7(5)) and the financial year (s 17).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation ("version in force from 1/4/2024"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/SPA1954.txt. The revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021";
-- the latest amendment annotated is Act 4 of 2008 (Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2008), annotated "wef 01/04/2024" on
-- s 7(3)(e)(v) and s 7A and listed in the legislative history with commencement 1 April 2024. Section numbers follow the body.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0213 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. SCOPED to the provisions a student, fee-payer, diploma holder, lender or counterparty meets, and the
-- governance rules that decide whether a decision affecting them was validly made. Not encoded: establishment and purposes (s 3),
-- the Board's general duty and functions beyond the by-law heads (s 7(1)-(3)), committees beyond s 7(5) (s 7(4), (6)), the
-- Secretary (s 8), presiding and standing orders (s 9(4)-(8)), contracts and property (s 10), investment (s 11(2), (3)), shares
-- issued to the Minister for Finance (s 11A), the Board of Studies (s 13), the Principal's responsibilities (s 14(2), (3)), other
-- officers (s 14A) and the regulation-making heads other than (d) and (e) (s 23(1)). No by-laws or regulations were retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Singapore Polytechnic Act 1954`

§§ `7(3)(d), (e) and 23 -- which instrument, and how it is made`

-- s 7(3): the Board's functions include "(d) the making, after consultation with the Board of Studies, of by-laws relating generally
-- to the academic management of the Polytechnic and in particular to -- (i) the qualifications necessary for admission to the
-- Polytechnic, the courses of instruction ..., the duration and number of Polytechnic terms, the award of certificates or diplomas
-- ... and the revocation of any certificates or diplomas so awarded; (ii) the grant of scholarships and studentships, and the
-- revocation of any such grant"; and "(e) the making of by-laws relating to -- (i) the procedure in regard to meetings ... (v) the fees
-- or charges to be payable by any person to the Polytechnic, including charges for the late payment of any such fee or charge".
-- s 23(1): "The Board may, with the approval of the Minister, make regulations for ... (d) the appointment, promotion, conduct,
-- disciplinary control, dismissal and termination of service of the academic and administrative staff ...; (e) the conduct and
-- disciplinary control of students". (2): "All regulations made under this section must be published in the Gazette."
-- The Act sets no approval or publication step for by-laws. s 7(3)(g) also lists "the welfare and discipline of teachers, staff and
-- students" among the Board's functions; the encoding sends student and staff discipline to s 23 because s 23 names them as subjects
-- for regulations (an INFERENCE about which head governs where the two overlap).
DECLARE Subject IS ONE OF
    `admission qualifications`
    `courses and terms`
    `award or revocation of a diploma`
    `scholarships and studentships`
    `fees and late-payment charges`
    `procedure at meetings`
    `student conduct and discipline`
    `staff conduct and dismissal`

DECLARE Instrument IS ONE OF
    `by-laws made after consulting the Board of Studies`
    `by-laws`
    `regulations approved by the Minister and published in the Gazette`

GIVEN `the subject` IS A Subject
GIVETH AN Instrument
`the instrument the Act provides` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the subject`
    WHEN `admission qualifications` THEN `by-laws made after consulting the Board of Studies`
    WHEN `courses and terms` THEN `by-laws made after consulting the Board of Studies`
    WHEN `award or revocation of a diploma` THEN `by-laws made after consulting the Board of Studies`
    WHEN `scholarships and studentships` THEN `by-laws made after consulting the Board of Studies`
    WHEN `fees and late-payment charges` THEN `by-laws`
    WHEN `procedure at meetings` THEN `by-laws`
    OTHERWISE `regulations approved by the Minister and published in the Gazette`

-- Whether a failure to publish in the Gazette invalidates a regulation is not said; the rule below reports only whether the steps the
-- Act names were taken.
GIVEN `the subject` IS A Subject, `the Board of Studies was consulted` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister approved` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instrument was made with the steps the Act names` IF
    CONSIDER `the instrument the Act provides` `the subject`
    WHEN `by-laws made after consulting the Board of Studies` THEN `the Board of Studies was consulted`
    WHEN `by-laws` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `regulations approved by the Minister and published in the Gazette` THEN `the Minister approved` AND `published in the Gazette`

§§ `7(3)(e)(v) and 7A -- late-payment charges`

-- s 7(3)(e)(v), quoted above, "including charges for the late payment" [Act 4 of 2008 wef 01/04/2024].
-- s 7A: "Every amount collected before the date of commencement of the Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2008 as, or purportedly
-- as, a charge for the late payment of any fee or charge referred to in section 7(2)(e)(v) shall be deemed to be and always to have
-- been validly collected, and no legal proceedings shall lie or be instituted or maintained in any court of law on account of or in
-- respect of any such collection." A footnote says "Section 7(2)(e)(v) is to be construed as section 7(3)(e)(v)".
-- The legislative history gives that Act's commencement as 1 April 2024. Dates are written as yyyymmdd numbers.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the commencement of Act 4 of 2008` MEANS 20240401

GIVEN `collected on` IS A NUMBER, `collected as a late-payment charge on a Polytechnic fee or charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 7A deems the collection valid and bars proceedings` IF
        `collected as a late-payment charge on a Polytechnic fee or charge`
    AND `collected on` LESS THAN `the commencement of Act 4 of 2008`

-- From commencement, by-laws may provide for late-payment charges in terms (s 7(3)(e)(v)).
GIVEN `charged on` IS A NUMBER, `provided for by by-laws` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 7(3)(e)(v) expressly covers the late-payment charge` IF
    `provided for by by-laws` AND `charged on` AT LEAST `the commencement of Act 4 of 2008`

§§ `12 -- the common seal`

-- s 12: "The common seal of the Board must be in the custody of the Principal and must not be affixed to any instrument, other than
-- diplomas or academic certificates, except in the presence of the Chairperson or a member of the Board, and the Principal, nor until
-- the Chairperson or the member of the Board, and the Principal, have signed their names to the instrument in token of their
-- presence."
GIVEN `a diploma or academic certificate` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Principal was present and signed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Chairperson or another Board member was present and signed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the seal may be affixed` IF
        `a diploma or academic certificate`
    OR  (`the Principal was present and signed` AND `the Chairperson or another Board member was present and signed`)

§§ `15, 16 -- the Students' Union`

-- s 15(3): "The Board may impose and collect from the students or any class of students such fees as it may determine for the benefit
-- of the Singapore Polytechnic Students' Union and its constituent bodies; and the fees may be applied in any manner that the Board
-- thinks fit for the purposes of the Union and its constituent bodies."
-- s 16(1): "Despite anything to the contrary in the Societies Act 1966, the provisions of that Act apply to" the Union and its
-- constituent bodies constituted by regulations under s 23(1); (2): the Minister charged with societies "may, by order in the Gazette,
-- exempt" them "from all or any of the provisions" of that Act, subject to conditions.
GIVEN `for the purposes of the Union or its constituent bodies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Union fee may be applied to the use` IF `for the purposes of the Union or its constituent bodies`

GIVEN `constituted by regulations under section 23(1)` IS A BOOLEAN, `exempted from that provision by Gazette order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Societies Act provision applies to the body` IF
    `constituted by regulations under section 23(1)` AND (NOT `exempted from that provision by Gazette order`)

§§ `11(1) -- borrowing`

-- s 11(1): "The Board may borrow at interest, on the security of any corporate land or of any funds of the Board, moneys that it may
-- think necessary or expedient for carrying into effect the provisions of this Act." No approval of the Minister for Finance is
-- required. Reading s 11(1) as authorising only secured borrowing is an INFERENCE (s 11(3) lets the Board "do anything incidental or
-- appertaining to a body corporate").
GIVEN `for carrying the Act into effect` IS A BOOLEAN, `secured on corporate land or Board funds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 11(1) authorises the loan` IF
    `for carrying the Act into effect` AND `secured on corporate land or Board funds`

§§ `4, 5, 6 -- the Board's size, terms and vacancies`

-- s 4(2): the Board is "(a) a Chairperson; (b) a Deputy Chairperson; (c) the Principal; and (d) such other persons, not being less than 9
-- or more than 15, as the Minister may determine". (3): every member "except the Principal" is appointed by the Minister and "unless
-- the Minister otherwise directs, holds office for a period of 3 years" and is eligible for re-appointment.
-- s 5(1): "The office of a member of the Board is vacated if the member -- (a) becomes a bankrupt or suspends payment to, or makes any
-- arrangement or composition with, his or her creditors; or (b) has been absent, without leave of the Board, from 3 consecutive
-- meetings of the Board." Unlike (2) and (3), (1) does not except the Principal.
-- s 5(2): the Minister may revoke an appointment, "except that of the Principal", if the member "becomes in the opinion of the Minister
-- unfit to continue in office or incapable of performing the member's duties"; (3) a member, "except the Principal", may resign by
-- written notice to the Minister.
-- s 6: if an office "other than that of the Principal" is vacant, the Minister "may appoint any person to fill the vacancy and to hold
-- the office for the remainder of the term of the person's predecessor".
DECLARE Member IS ONE OF
    `the Chairperson`
    `the Deputy Chairperson`
    `the Principal`
    `an appointed member`

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member is the Principal` IF
    CONSIDER `the member`
    WHEN `the Principal` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board has a lawful number of members` IF
    `members` AT LEAST 12 AND `members` AT MOST 18

GIVEN `the Minister directed another term` IS A BOOLEAN, `directed term in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the term of an appointed member in years` MEANS
    IF `the Minister directed another term` THEN `directed term in years` ELSE 3

GIVEN `predecessor's term in years` IS A NUMBER, `years the predecessor served` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the replacement's term in years` MEANS
    `predecessor's term in years` MINUS `years the predecessor served`

GIVEN `insolvency event` IS A BOOLEAN, `consecutive meetings missed without leave` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the office is vacated` IF
    `insolvency event` OR `consecutive meetings missed without leave` AT LEAST 3

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member, `the Minister thinks the member unfit or incapable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may revoke the appointment` IF
    (NOT `the member is the Principal` `the member`) AND `the Minister thinks the member unfit or incapable`

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member may resign by written notice to the Minister` IF
    NOT `the member is the Principal` `the member`

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may fill the vacancy` IF
    NOT `the member is the Principal` `the member`

§§ `9 -- Board meetings and votes`

-- s 9(2): "At every meeting of the Board 6 members form a quorum." (3): decisions by "a simple majority of the votes of the members
-- present and voting, except that in the case of an equality of votes, the Chairperson or, in the Chairperson's absence, the Deputy
-- Chairperson of the Board has a casting vote". (5): if both are absent, a member elected by those present presides -- but s 9(3) gives
-- that member no casting vote. The encoding reads a tie with both absent as NOT carried (an INFERENCE: the text does not say).
GIVEN `present` IS A NUMBER, `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER,
      `the Chairperson is present` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Deputy Chairperson is present` IS A BOOLEAN, `the casting vote is for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board motion is carried` IF
        `present` AT LEAST 6
    AND (   `votes for` GREATER THAN `votes against`
         OR (    `votes for` EQUALS `votes against`
             AND (`the Chairperson is present` OR `the Deputy Chairperson is present`)
             AND `the casting vote is for`))

§§ `7(5), 14(1), (4) -- committees and the Principal`

-- s 7(5): "The proceedings of every committee of the Board must be recorded in writing and must be open to the inspection of any member
-- of the Board or any member of the committee at any time." The Act gives no one else a right to inspect.
-- s 14(4): the Principal "is entitled to be present and speak at any meeting of any committee of the Board, but is not entitled to
-- vote at the meeting unless the Principal is a member of the committee".
-- s 14(1): the Principal is appointed by the Board "and the Principal may for good cause be removed from office by the Board"; (2):
-- removal "must be in accordance with the Public Sector (Governance) Act 2018" (not encoded).
DECLARE Inquirer IS ONE OF
    `a Board member`
    `a committee member`
    `a student`
    `a member of the public`

GIVEN `the inquirer` IS AN Inquirer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the inquirer may inspect the committee's proceedings` IF
    CONSIDER `the inquirer`
    WHEN `a Board member` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a committee member` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `a member of the committee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Principal may vote at the committee meeting` IF `a member of the committee`

GIVEN `good cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may remove the Principal` IF `good cause`

§§ `17 -- the financial year`

-- s 17: "The financial year of the Polytechnic begins on 1 April of each year and ends on 31 March of the succeeding year."
GIVEN `calendar year` IS A NUMBER, `month number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year in which the financial year began` MEANS
    IF `month number` AT LEAST 4 THEN `calendar year` ELSE `calendar year` MINUS 1
